  "title": "Balancer · Level 2: Hold your place under three pushes",
  "brief": "The balancing robot (a rig, not the class robot: EV3 Large motors on ports 1-2, left mirrored on 1, 56 mm wheels 150 mm apart, an IMU on I2C 8) starts held upright within 3 deg and is released at the Run. Balance for 30 s and hold your place through three pushes, each drawn per run: 100, 150 or 200 mN s, forward or backward, horizontal at the body's centre of mass (120 mm above the axle), one at a whole second from 4 to 8 s, one from 13 to 17 s and one from 22 to 26 s. The reference program recovers from every push the level can draw. Practice: the fall end and the score (100 - RMS position error (mm) / 2, 0 on a fall) wait for the body truth (GT); the run is not scored yet.",
